{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/13267","id":5453305776,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABRQrXsA","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/13267","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/13267.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/13267.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/13267","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/13267/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/13267/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/13267/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/0b344c9d23bbd92ab1400ab3a66c8c9825bbf887","number":13267,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(id): kitty keyboard slices E+F — SSH negotiation/framing and browser opt-in (#787)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Implements the two remaining slices of #787 per `doc/2026-11-01_design_id787.md` §6. Slices A–D were already on main (Roc decoder #4438, assembler, browser encoder #7734, parity oracle #12926), and the F13.4 startup probe already records `kitty_keyboard` support in the SSH adapter — this PR wires activation to that evidence. **This PR does not close #787**: the issue's final acceptance also wants one supported-terminal smoke session (and the unsupported fallback) recorded against a real terminal, which a remote test run cannot supply.\n\n## Slice E — opt-in SSH lifecycle integration (`world_ssh`)\n\n- New `SshServeOptions { kitty_keyboard }` (default off); `serve()` delegates to `serve_with_options()`. The serve command maps env `ID_WORLD_SSH_KITTY_KEYBOARD=1` to it, following the existing `ID_WORLD_*` env pattern, with a status line when enabled.\n- On a raw session (never command/explorer/exec), after the F13.4 probe closes with uncontradicted kitty support, the session writes the profile push `CSI > 1 u` + flags query `CSI ? u` and **verifies before admitting any key**: tokens assembled during verification are held; a flags report carrying the disambiguation bit activates framing, one without it — or a 500 ms timeout — pops the owned push and falls back to legacy chunk input with held bytes untouched. One attempt per connection (no renegotiation loop).\n- While active, input runs through the Slice B assembler: one complete key token per durable `Input` event, exact bytes preserved, split/CSI/UTF-8 safe. Verification replies are consumed by an outstanding-query-only filter — never journaled. Framing errors, incomplete token at EOF/deadline, and input-queue loss past the activation baseline are fatal to the session (no unsafe resync).\n- Teardown pops exactly the owned push on every exit path (normal, refused, error, cancellation) before the alternate screen is left. Form answers route through the same engaged stream so the assembler cannot desync around them.\n- The assembler module moves from the `id` facade into `id-worlds` (the adapter's crate); the facade re-exports it, so `id::input_framing` is unchanged.\n\n## Slice F — browser opt-in (`web`)\n\n- `world.ts` selects `richTerminalBytesForKey` per connection when the page is opened with `?keyboard=kitty`; legacy stays the default. Paste, the manual input form, and Meta/Dead/Process exclusions are unchanged in both modes.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `world_ssh::kitty` unit tests: flags-report grammar, outstanding-only consumption, verify flip/refusal, coalesced key order, fallback byte fidelity, split tokens.\n- `world_ssh` integration tests (real russh client + world event subscription): negotiate → verify → split CSI-u framed as one event, Escape vs Alt+x as distinct events, no reply bytes journaled, exactly one pop at teardown; verification-refused fallback (held key delivered, legacy resumes, no second push); no negotiation without the opt-in; no push when the terminal reports no support.\n- Web: new `world-keyboard-optin.test.ts` — DOM → WebSocket in both modes (legacy bare Escape `1b` vs kitty `CSI 27 u`, Ctrl+i vs Tab, Alt+x), paste + shortcut exclusions under the opt-in.\n\n## Verification state (read this before merging)\n\nRemote dispatches were queued while runner surfaces were exhausted; all three were still `queued` (no surface) when this PR was opened. Handles (branch head `00520a8a3`):\n\n- Rust tests (`cargo test -p id-worlds --features ssh world_ssh` + `input_framing`): `fp_250be4a8258466cd46be42840fee197b`\n- Web tests + typecheck: `fp_b7b9a7f0f820ca7eb716a93e47b95c1a`\n- Clippy (`id-worlds`, `id-cli`, `id`, all targets/features): `fp_ac36488f6ba6798b5a8af6a3cba2b93e`\n\nThe jobs are recorded in the fleet queue and run when a surface frees; results land under `fleet queue session result <handle>`. Local verification was rustfmt only (remote-builds-only rule). No new dependencies.\n\n## Residuals named in the design\n\n- Queue-loss fatality is observed on the recv path against the activation baseline; a drop claimed by the send path's viewer notice in the same instant could in principle race it — the window is one loop iteration and the failure mode degrades to today's legacy notice behavior.\n- Disambiguation only, per the design: no event-type/all-keys/alternate-key flags, no keyup path.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://dashboardbackend.blacksmith.sh/track/run-proof?expires=1798029673&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=13267&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F13267&variant=proof_this_pr&signature=b158d47dc21faed932ec6e33b3682ebd04bbdd63e07c2b075c8b5b99f22d588e\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/proof-proof-this-pr-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/proof-proof-this-pr-v2-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Proof this PR\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/proof-proof-this-pr-v2-dark-3x.png\" width=\"121\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/13267?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added optional kitty keyboard support for browser sessions, enabled with `?keyboard=kitty`. Other sessions continue to use legacy keyboard input.\n  * Added opt-in kitty keyboard negotiation for SSH sessions. When the terminal supports it, key input is assembled into complete key events; unsupported terminals continue using legacy input.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved handling of incomplete or unverified keyboard input, preserving buffered input when SSH sessions fall back to legacy behavior.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","labels":[{"id":13198400136,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAADEq-aiA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/audit:complete","name":"audit:complete","description":"PR fully implemented spawning issue","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-23T12:41:08Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T02:07:11Z","closed_at":"2026-11-23T20:51:57Z","merged_at":"2026-11-23T20:51:57Z","merge_commit_sha":"b8b903b24b603e35ac5f12b4d7c6a77f57472768","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"developing-today:felix/787-kitty-slice-e-f","ref":"felix/787-kitty-slice-e-f","repo":{"id":627308783,"node_id":"R_kgDOJWP47w","name":"code","full_name":"developing-today/code","owner":{"login":"developing-today","id":26439447,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjI2NDM5NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developin